#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0216 expect=violation domain=SV
#note "B2 CONTROL of PLAN-unplanned-visit-cascade: no SVPRESP column. Under the pre-cascade empty(SVPRESP) form rows 1, 3 AND the whole dataset's populated-VISITDY rows FIRED (absent column folds to all-empty - the flood this plan retires); under the cascade row 1 is planned (blank SVUPDES, neutral name) and keeps its VISITDY. Row 2 (populated SVUPDES) and row 3 (UNPLANNED marker) are unplanned with VISITDY populated -> fire. Row 4 has no VISITDY -> clean. This fixture reds under the old form (row 1 in the count)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-3
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-701-1015
#expectViolationAt row=3 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SVSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVUPDES  type=Char label="Description of Unplanned Visit"
col VISITDY  type=Num  label="Planned Study Day of Visit"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 1 | 2 | BASELINE |  | 14
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 2 | 99 | WEEK 99 | POST-AE EXTRA VISIT | 1
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 3 | 98 | UNPLANNED 2 |  | 2
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 4 | 1 | SCREENING |  | 
---
